# The CPLM copy pointer on the factorial's candidate (factorial.bux's r1v1k1f0p0s0: the
# late-2026 hybrid with hyper-connections, the value residual and the key-value conv):
# its head's next-token distribution mixed with a pointer over the earlier tokens of
# the document. A file of its own, as the pointer is a setting of the shared head,
# whose second call, the MTP module's, keeps its plain softmax. Arms: era, source,
# what it was claimed for.
use m2026_hybrid
use timeline_code
use rungs

# 2026 modded-nanogpt PR 379 (CPLM): a <copy> row of the head, whose mass a goes to a
# 128-d pointer over the document's earlier final hidden states, p = p_lm (1 - a) +
# a p_copy; 12% fewer steps at 124M, the most direct lever for repository bpb
shared fr_out = nl_cplm: head(pointer=copy_pointer()) | nl_cplm_w4k: head(pointer=copy_pointer(window=4096))

g_k   = fr_global(kv_conv_size=4)
model = embed
        fr_layer(hy_delta, fr_dense) fr_layer(hy_delta)^2 fr_layer(g_k(v=@v1))
        (fr_layer(hy_delta)^3 fr_layer(g_k(v=$v1)))^(layers // 4 - 1)
        fr_norm @h fr_out hy_mtp
residual = hc(expansion=4)

# The hybrid's best at d512 (milestones.bux's scan), for every arm.
optimizer.lr = 2e-3
